# LinkedIn Feed Stability Rule

## Workflow
- Run RCA in single-stage iterations only (no all-at-once analysis).
- After each stage, stop and wait for user confirmation ("continue").
- Do not revisit already confirmed stages unless explicitly requested.
- Prefer minimal targeted fixes; avoid broad refactors.

## Stage Order
1. Page Load / Navigation
2. Scroll Logic
3. DOM / Selectors
4. Async / Timing
5. Data Extraction
6. Retry / Stability

## Critical Guardrails
- If feed readiness times out and post anchors count is zero, escalate as failure.
- In scroll loops, treat progress as data growth (`after_len > before_len`), not just scroll movement.
- Trigger retry on repeated empty-feed / empty-read states.
- Add local retry (2-3 attempts) for `post_url` extraction after copy-link action.
- If primary text anchor is absent, use selector fallback for `read_posts`.
- Avoid noisy container matches unless container has post-like signals.

## Required Diagnostics
- Log `url_source` (`dom|menu|none`), `url_found`, `container_key`, and `attempt`.
- Log per-iteration `before_len`, `after_len`, and stagnation counters.

## Good vs Bad
- Bad: Continue parsing right after readiness timeout with zero anchors.
- Good: Fail fast, retry once, then parse only when anchors/data appear.
